 "text": "[gentle music] Most docs readers are now AI agents. An intuitive, intentional docs interface becomes even more important. General Translation redesigned its docs from scratch so people would read its writing. Interfaces keep getting more cluttered, which creates mental clutter. The redesign started by deleting extra lines, links, and buttons. The sidebar is now one accordion, which is rare among doc sites. The writing now has more open space around it. Translated pages keep the same spacing and alignment. Each page guides its reader toward the action they want. Docs design is an open problem, and the team keeps working on it. [gentle music]",
